From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] est: estimate_parasitics without a flag picks the source

A flow that times a design has to say -placement or -global_routing,
so every flow script that loads a design re-derives which one applies:
from a stage number, from grt::have_routes, from whether a .spef file
is on disk. Each copy can get it wrong, and a missing piece fails
quietly: -placement without wire RC only warns (EST-0018), and a
congested global route that was not accepted makes -global_routing
fail with EST-0005, "Run global_route", after global_route ran.

Without a flag, estimate_parasitics estimates from the global routes
when there are any, else from placement, and does nothing once
read_spef has read parasitics, until an estimate with a flag replaces
them. An unplaced design (EST-0009), global routes that are congested
and were not accepted (EST-0020) and a placement estimate without wire
RC (EST-0014) are errors. -placement and -global_routing behave as
before, except that a congested route fails with EST-0008, which names
the congestion. grt::have_congested_routes, grt::design_is_placed and
est::parasitics_source let a flow ask.

The two commits of an OpenROAD pull request, squashed. Retires at the
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it; 0137 depends on it.
---
diff --git a/src/est/README.md b/src/est/README.md
index 2b2b4035c7..faeec0084b 100644
--- a/src/est/README.md
+++ b/src/est/README.md
@@ -146,15 +146,23 @@ Standard Parasitic Exchange Format.
 
 ```tcl
 estimate_parasitics
-    -placement|-global_routing
+    [-placement|-global_routing]
     [-spef_file spef_file]
 ```
 
+Without `-placement` or `-global_routing`, `estimate_parasitics` estimates
+from what the design has: from the global routes when there are any, else
+from placement. It does nothing once `read_spef` has read parasitics, until
+`estimate_parasitics -placement` or `-global_routing` replaces them. An
+unplaced design, global routes that are congested and were not accepted with
+`global_route -allow_congestion`, and a placement estimate without wire RC
+are errors.
+
 #### Options
 
 | Switch Name | Description |
 | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
-| `-placement` or `-global_routing` | Either of these flags must be set. Parasitics are estimated based after placement stage versus after global routing stage. |
+| `-placement` or `-global_routing` | Optional. Parasitics are estimated from placement or from global routing. Without either, the design decides. |
 | `-spef_file` | Optional. File name to write SPEF files. If more than one corner is available for the design, the files will be written as filename_corner.spef. |
 
 
